      "created_at": "2015-03-10T11:51:12.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was reading a very interesting article on the BBC website today about <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/business-31506073\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">the practical application of ammonia heat pumps</a>. Right down the bottom there is mention that the RIver Thames could be used to generate 1.25 GW of thermal energy and immediately I thought \"Great Scott! That's more than enough to power the DeLorean!\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Actually, the fact that I was reading that article in the first place totally makes me a geek.</p>",
